        2,
        3
      ],
      "devanagari": "वनानि गिरयो नद्यो दुर्गाणि गहनानि च |\nदरी गिरि गुहाः चैव विचिता नः समंततः\nतत्र तत्र सह अस्माभिः जानकी न च दृश्यते |\nतथा रक्षः अपहर्ता च सीतायाः चैव दुष्कृती",
      "iast": "vanāni girayo nadyo dur.hgāṇi gahanāni ca |\ndarī giri guhāḥ caiva vicitā naḥ samaṃtataḥ\ntatra tatra saha asmābhiḥ jānakī na ca dṛśyate |\ntathā rakṣaḥ apahartā ca sītāyāḥ caiva duṣ.hkṛtī",
      "translation": "\"We in oneness have searched there and thereabouts in the impassable forests, mountains, and rivers, and unfathomable cavities and in mountain caves up to their end, but we have not seen Janaki, so also that ill-natured demon, the abductor of Seetha, is not seen.",
